                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cd8398c-5393-391f-bef6-6456a891662c",
                        "entry_id": "bf65c569-cb93-32aa-8392-8c3975c1b539",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stützstruktur, die eine stabile äußere Hülle um einen Organismus bildet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67b73ab3-55dc-4d6d-836e-60b556233b96",
                                "sense_id": "2cd8398c-5393-391f-bef6-6456a891662c",
                                "text": "„Das Außenskelett der Arthropodenbeine besteht aus dünnwandigen, röhrenförmige Komponenten, die durch Gelenke miteinander verbunden sind.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa281d3c-7034-4cd9-8d0b-9aff5bb9cd8c",
                        "source_entry_id": "bf65c569-cb93-32aa-8392-8c3975c1b539",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cd8398c-5393-391f-bef6-6456a891662c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Biologie: Stützstruktur, die eine stabile äußere Hülle um einen Organismus bildet",
                        "target_lang_word": "exoskeleton",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exoskeleton",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b457c778-23e4-3e5d-b28f-dd2426841c1f",
                                        "entry_id": "b89fa933-294a-34b0-a18d-26c2d60688ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hard outer structure that provides both structure and protection to creatures such as insects and Crustacea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bc0ddcd-44ec-455d-b1df-68d900a5471c",
                                                "sense_id": "b457c778-23e4-3e5d-b28f-dd2426841c1f",
                                                "text": "This is the case not only with all forms provided with exoskeleta and endoskeleta, into the composition of which lime largely enters, but also with those which exercise the precipitating effect on the calcium salts they absorb from sea water, the precipitation rarely going so far as to form a distinct deposit in the cells or tissues of the organism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d35be9d-544d-45a2-9a18-4fd37ad26f81",
                                                "sense_id": "b457c778-23e4-3e5d-b28f-dd2426841c1f",
                                                "text": "Ordinarily, allergy to animals is due to either their fine dander which becomes aerosolized or to the exoskeleta, pupae, or feces of their ectoparasites."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcb734f4-02d3-423a-8d97-56e996bca527",
                                                "sense_id": "b457c778-23e4-3e5d-b28f-dd2426841c1f",
                                                "text": "After separation, the next generation of daughters resumes the photosynthetic fixation (reduction) of carbon, the sequestration of phosphorus, nitrogen, and mineral nutrients (up to a score), and the synthesis of the proteins that will contribute to the generational doubling of biomass. Structures such as flagella, scales, and exoskeleta also have to be reallocated or copied."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7162378-2c0d-4869-93b1-8ba3fb959c7d",
                                                "sense_id": "b457c778-23e4-3e5d-b28f-dd2426841c1f",
                                                "text": "Drawings supplied with NR's council application show a bridge with an exoskeleton that repeats some of the angles of Hitachi's '800' series trains which LNER and TransPennine Express run through the station."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4e0f4e1-6347-313a-a329-cb2b9e4347e1",
                                        "entry_id": "b89fa933-294a-34b0-a18d-26c2d60688ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wearable robotic machine used for aided or augmented mobility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "037804db-ff6c-4a11-8028-c0d82697fae5",
                        "source_entry_id": "bf65c569-cb93-32aa-8392-8c3975c1b539",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cd8398c-5393-391f-bef6-6456a891662c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Biologie: Stützstruktur, die eine stabile äußere Hülle um einen Organismus bildet",
                        "target_lang_word": "exosquelette",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exosquelette",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a38c8cfe-b012-317c-9439-e5a3280c25f9",
                                        "entry_id": "636c2076-7534-3ed3-a54a-571f8fa43888",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Structure anatomique externe qui protège certains invertébrés."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9f6fc29-a15c-4302-b833-8fd2ed429cbb",
                                                "sense_id": "a38c8cfe-b012-317c-9439-e5a3280c25f9",
                                                "text": "On peut prendre l’orvet (anguis fragilis) pour type des vertébrés dont l’exosquelette et l'endosquelette coexistent et sont édifiés sur un plan dont la régularité et la continuité ne laissent absolument rien à désirer pour l'étude."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7dbf01e4-8e80-3a9f-be88-dfa457d4f643",
                                        "entry_id": "636c2076-7534-3ed3-a54a-571f8fa43888",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Armature technique augmentant les capacités d’une personne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "analogy"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5496f4c7-de05-4e2b-9a4e-e388133fb216",
                                                "sense_id": "7dbf01e4-8e80-3a9f-be88-dfa457d4f643",
                                                "text": "Nous testons ces exosquelettes dans de nombreuses usines, comme celle de Munich : ils soulagent les ouvriers effectuant des tâches répétitives sur les chaînes d’assemblage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77fa4344-2615-4545-a18f-59deff4ac356",
                                                "sense_id": "7dbf01e4-8e80-3a9f-be88-dfa457d4f643",
                                                "text": "L’univers de la supply chain voit arriver des « robots collaboratifs » (cobots) qui associent l’homme et la machine, des flottes de robots, des drones, des exosquelettes (pour soulager le corps du poids de la charge) et une multitude d’innovations technologiques, numériques, ultra-connectées, de petites machines polyvalentes, sans cesse renouvelées, qui fraient avec les humains dans ces entrepôts, « boîtes noires » du flux de la mondialisation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
